To force a text field to display text in columns using Adobe JavaScript, you can use the `setColumns` method of the `TextField` class. Here's an example of how you might do this:

```javascript
// Assuming you have a text field with the instance name 'myTextField'
var myTextField = this.myTextField;

// Set the number of columns you want to display
var numColumns = 2; // Change this to the number of columns you want

// Set the columns for the text field
myTextField.setColumns(numColumns);
```

This code snippet sets the number of columns for the text field with the instance name 'myTextField' to 2. You can change the value of `numColumns` to any number you want to display the text in that many columns.

